WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
The Buddha taught by speaking.

2
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.080
He wrote nothing down.

3
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.850
Yet today Buddhists study a
vast collection of discourses,

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.820
rules and teachings,
sorted into 3 baskets.

5
00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:17.750
And in 1967, Martin Luther King Jr nominated
a Vietnamese monk for the Nobel Peace

6
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.880
Prize.

7
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.880
So where do Buddhists find
the Buddha's teaching,

8
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.750
and whose voices still guide them today?

9
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.730
In this mission, you'll open the 3 baskets
and read verses from the Dhammapada.

10
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.820
Then you'll meet Thich Nhat Hanh, and
weigh up whether his teaching still matters

11
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:34.930
today.

12
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.830
Your mission: find out where
Buddhists find the Buddha's teaching,

13
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.750
and whose voice still guides them.
